- op: discuss  # fde5
  at: '2026-04-27T04:01:38Z'  # fde5
  by: agent  # fde5
  actor: jgstern_agent  # fde5
  clock: 20  # fde5
  nonce: fde5  # fde5
  message: "Acknowledged all three decisions; proceeding with implementation on a feature branch. Concrete plan locked from your decisions:\n\n(1) Verification gate at the close-and-repush boundary in scripts/auto-pr Scenario B path — both checks: _check_pr_merged for the merged-during-timeout sub-case, AND a small wrapper composing api_get on /pulls/<n> with a single retry of poll_ci+backoff for the about-to-merge poll-flake sub-case. ~10-20 lines, no new helpers, no gh dependency. Existing primitives in forgejo-api.sh.\n\n(2) Post-rebase poll-and-merge as a labeled while-loop with continue and a max-iter cap (2-3) inside do_merge() in scripts/lib/forgejo-api.sh. NOT recursion — that creates the AUTOPR_FROM_REBASE re-entry hazard you flagged. Greppable shape: while [ \"$attempts\" -lt 3 ]; do ...; rebase+force-push; continue; done. After force-push of the rebased SHA, re-enter poll_ci on the new SHA before re-attempting merge.\n\n(3) On ship, status will move to pending_validation with the validation criterion verbatim: 'the next auto-pr invocation that traverses the rebase-then-merge path completes without emitting Recovery: and merges to dev.' Naturally exercised; no synthetic reproducer.\n\nStatus flip now: needs_human_review → violated (active-fix). Will report PR # in a follow-up entry once auto-pr lands the change. Both files touched (scripts/auto-pr, scripts/lib/forgejo-api.sh) are governance-listed; the explicit decisions in the prior message constitute the human approval the governance protocol requires."  # fde5
