  message: "[Wave-0 pending-validation sweep] \ntracker: keep pending INV-rahib, validation verified via static code inspection and property tests\n\nBoth surfaces of the fix (PR #3419, commit da94238c98) are present and correct:\n\nSurface 1 - pre-Scenario-B gate (_pre_scenario_b_gate in forgejo-api.sh:1337-1370):\n  - Calls _check_pr_merged (line 1342) for merged-during-timeout sub-case\n  - Calls api_get + mergeable + poll_ci-retry-120s (lines 1348-1366) for about-to-merge poll-flake sub-case\n  - Used at timeout-recovery (auto-pr, before close-and-repush) and hung-run loop (auto-pr, each iteration)\n\nSurface 2 - post-rebase poll-and-merge loop (forgejo-api.sh:1193-1232):\n  - Labeled while loop with rebase_max=3 iterations (Decision 2: labeled loop NOT recursion)\n  - Re-polls CI on post-rebase SHA (line 1199: poll_ci \"$new_sha\")\n  - Explicit continue for re-rebase case (line 1220)\n  - Recovery: hint ONLY after loop exhaustion (line 1240, gated by rebase_merged=false at line 1234)\n\nTest coverage: test_autopr_rahib_convergence.py 16/16 pass (pre-commit hook style, seam-driven subprocess tests for gate helper).\n\nValidation criterion: \"the next auto-pr invocation that traverses the rebase-then-merge path completes without emitting Recovery: and merges to dev.\" This is organic validation requiring natural concurrent-activity trigger. Correctness strategy doc (2026-06-10) still lists as pending_validation, indicating this natural occurrence hasn't been observed since deploy (2026-04-27). Recommendation: keep pending_validation until a real auto-pr traversal is logged or a bakeoff-driven test explicitly exercises the path.\n"  # 1fdb
