- op: discuss  # dd66
  at: '2026-06-15T08:02:53Z'  # dd66
  by: agent  # dd66
  actor: jgstern_agent  # dd66
  clock: 30  # dd66
  nonce: dd66  # dd66
  message: "New reproduction 2026-06-15 (during projection:F1 / PR #242 ship; selfh failover active). DISTINCT path from the 2026-04-26 rebase-then-stop regression — this one is the hung-run heuristic firing a FALSE 'runners down'. Sequence: auto-pr opened PR #238; its 'No CI jobs have started after 300s -> possible hung runner (exit 3)' check fired because selfh runners were slow to PICK UP jobs (NOT down); it then closed/re-pushed across 4 hung-run retries (#238->#239->#240->#241->#242, ~30min) and exited 0 with 'Scenario C: CI runners may be down ... ./scripts/merge-pr 242 --wait-for-ci'. But the runners then ran ALL 13 jobs on #242 and they PASSED; ci-debug status showed Overall: success; merge-pr 242 --wait-for-ci fast-forwarded cleanly. This is the invariant's explicit 'misleading status (failure when CI passed)' violation, plus convergence to the WRONG terminal state (explicit-failure where the correct state was merged). Root: the 'no jobs started after Ns' timeout treats slow job-START as runner-death; it also churned 5 PRs by close-and-repush without first checking whether the existing PR was already green/about-to-merge. Recommended fix shape (HUMAN — scripts/auto-pr is a governance script; NOT self-assigning): before declaring hung-run/Scenario C, query PR state (statusCheckRollup / mergeable) to distinguish 'jobs slow to start' from 'runners down', and prefer waiting/merging an already-green PR over close-and-repush (mirrors the thread's earlier 'gh pr view before close-and-repush' suggestion). Status pending_validation -> violated: positive reproduction of a still-open violation via a path the prior fix did not cover."  # dd66
- op: discuss  # 9959
  at: '2026-06-17T07:15:34Z'  # 9959
  by: agent  # 9959
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9959
  clock: 31  # 9959
  nonce: '9959'  # 9959
  message: "Fresh instance (2026-06-17, human-observed). auto-pr on the WI-moriz PR did NOT converge: it ran hung-run retries (closed PR #260, re-pushed as #261), then exited 1 reporting 'CI Failed. Contexts: pytest / pytest-retry / ci-complete' — but ci-debug status for the same commit (f32afafd) showed Overall: PENDING with NO failed contexts (lint/mypy/dco/audit/hook-tests/stop-the-line/changes green, the rest still running). Root cause per human: the scheduled nightly (multi-Python matrix + integration, ~05:30 UTC) was running concurrently, creating duplicate/contended CI jobs — auto-pr's poll tripped over a duplicate failed/timed-out context while the real run was still alive. Recovery: merge-pr 261 --wait-for-ci (reused the in-progress run) merged cleanly once the nightly cleared. So auto-pr diverged to a FALSE explicit-failure under concurrent activity — the exact INV-rahib failure mode. Candidate hardening: auto-pr should distinguish a genuinely-failed required context from a transient/duplicate one (e.g., re-query status before declaring failure, or tolerate a context that has a sibling pending run) before exiting 1."  # 9959
