  message: "Fix MERGED (selfh/dev d738315910, via auto-pr per human approval of direction A + auto-pr without --gov). Surface 3: poll_ci now requires the failure-with-no-pending signal to be STABLE across FAILURE_CONFIRM_POLLS (default 2) consecutive polls before returning 1; the counter resets on any pending-sibling/in-progress poll. EVIDENCE: (1) behavioral tests in tests/test_autopr_rahib_convergence.py drive the REAL poll_ci loop against a scripted api_get sequence (CI_POLL_NO_SLEEP test knob) — a stable double-failure still returns 1 (genuine failures NOT masked); the incident shape (failure->pending->success) converges to 0 (no false failure). 3/3 new tests + 16 existing pass. (2) This very auto-pr merge ran WITH the fix active and converged cleanly (exit 0), though it did not hit concurrent contention so that is only a weak positive. PENDING_VALIDATION rather than satisfied: full validation requires observing auto-pr converge (no false explicit-failure) during a REAL concurrent-nightly run — the original failure condition. The two prior surfaces (2026-04-26 close-boundary gate; post-rebase re-poll) remain covered by their existing tests; this adds the third."  # 8003
