  message: "Priority P1 -> P2 (owner decision 2026-08-03). Status stays VIOLATED.\n\nRATIONALE. Every known surface now has a shipped fix: Surface 1 (mergeable read as a tri-state, re-query, green-CI deference) today in PR #180; Surface 2 (post-rebase poll-and-merge loop) 2026-04-27; Surface 3 (confirmation re-poll before declaring CI failed) 2026-06-17; plus WI-ninar replacing the dispatch predicate so a slow-to-start runner is no longer diagnosed as dead. There is NO CURRENTLY-REPRODUCING DEFECT on this item. The last positive reproduction was WI-buniz on 2026-08-01, which was itself fixed the same day.\n\nWhat remains is a VALIDATION OBLIGATION rather than a known-broken mechanism: observe, over a window of records in the new .git/AUTOPR_HISTORY.jsonl ledger, that no run carries final_state unknown and that every failure-bucket record agrees with ci-debug status for its SHA. That is passive observation, not P1-shaped work, and priority in this tracker orders what to work NEXT rather than how severe a failure would be.\n\nTHE COUNTER-ARGUMENT, recorded rather than waved away, because it is the stronger-sounding one. This invariant governs the tool that merges every PR, and a failure here has historically merged unrun code (PR #160 merged with CI still pending). It has also regressed THREE TIMES after being marked satisfied: satisfied 2026-03-31, regressed 2026-04-26; a distinct false hung-run path 2026-06-15; a false CI-failure path 2026-06-17; and the WI-buniz non-fast-forward misdiagnosis 2026-08-01. Its SEVERITY is not dropping. What has dropped is the evidence of an active defect, and those are different quantities. Anyone re-reading this should not take P2 as a claim that the invariant is nearly satisfied -- it is not, and the clause it remains violated on is named in the preceding entry.\n\nRE-ESCALATION TRIGGER (R10/R16 -- a downgrade carries the same burden as a KEEP verdict): return to P1 on any of (a) a ledger record with final_state unknown, (b) a fourth distinct surface reproducing in the wild, or (c) any auto-pr run that merges with CI not green. Trigger (a) is now executable for the first time, which is the substantive change that makes this downgrade defensible at all: before the ledger there was no artifact that could ever fire it."  # ac65
